    /* Treat product as 256 bits P[255:0] = X1 || X0 where bit 0 is the least
       significant bit of the low 64 of X0 (clmul convention). GHASH reflected
       multiply of byte-swapped inputs needs exactly this reduction:

       for i in 0..127: if bit i of low set, xor poly<<i into the 256-bit value,
       poly = 0x87 (i.e. bits 7,2,1,0 of the high half... ).

